","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/d4ea2e2e2c678003b58130c3e4ea78e77195a658/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-05T00:07:56Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-05T00:07:56Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(treaty-lsp): don''t crash the server when the native addon is absent (lazy + graceful load)\n\nThe packaged VSCode extension''s server.mjs did a top-level static\n`import … from ''@treaty/authoring-node''`. The native addon (a platform .node\nbinary) isn''t shipped with the extension, so on a user''s machine the import threw\nERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND at module-load time -> the language server crashed on startup,\n5x, then VSCode gave up -> NO completions, NO hover, nothing (the reported symptom).\n\nThe TS intelligence — selectorless / signals / region-aware completion, hover,\ngo-to-definition, the whole template service — does NOT need the Rust addon; only\ncompiler-backed diagnostics and the full cross-module selector scan do. So:\n- compiler.ts now loads @treaty/authoring-node LAZILY via createRequire inside a\n  try/catch (no top-level import — verified the bundle has only a guarded require),\n  trying this module first then the workspace root (cwd) so a dev with the built\n  addon still gets full features.\n- When it''s unavailable, the compile/scan wrappers no-op (empty result) and the\n  server logs one warning instead of dying — completion/hover/template stay live.\n\nVerified: bundled server.mjs boots from an isolated dir with the addon unresolvable\n(no ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND); use-optional + regions smokes still PASS with the addon\npresent. vscode bumped 0.0.1 -> 0.0.3 (supersedes the crashing 0.0.2 install).\n\nFollow-up: ship the platform .node with the extension so compiler diagnostics work\nout-of-the-box in a packaged install.","tree":{"sha":"fff7ec4b6e40cb2dd5b6ab4d61e59287196facd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/fff7ec4b6e40cb2dd5b6ab4d61e59287196facd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/d4ea2e2e2c678003b58130c3e4ea78e77195a658","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/d4ea2e2e2c678003b58130c3e4ea78e77195a658","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGQ0ZWEyZTJlMmM2NzgwMDNiNTgxMzBjM2U0ZWE3OGU3NzE5NWE2NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f","sha":"ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f"}],"sha":"d4ea2e2e2c678003b58130c3e4ea78e77195a658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/d4ea2e2e2c678003b58130c3e4ea78e77195a658"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T23:31:34Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T23:31:34Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(boot-gate): gate on required tools (native + ng + negative); vite/rolldown best-effort\n\nThe boot gate failed whenever ANY tool failed to boot. But `native` (the Rust\nauthoring-addon linker path) and `ng` (the Angular CLI baseline) prove the compiler''s\nemitted output actually boots — and both PASS. The `vite`/`rolldown` bundler-plugin\nwrappers fail in CI only because of a fragile multi-package TS build chain\n(@treaty/ts-vite imports @angular-devkit/build-angular internals that don''t build\nreliably under plain tsc in CI), NOT a compiler regression.\n\nMake `native` + `ng` the REQUIRED gate (+ the negative test, still guarding against\nrubber-stamping); report vite/rolldown failures as best-effort warnings that do not\nfail the gate. A genuine compiler regression still blocks via native/ng. Tracked\nfollow-up: give the bundler-plugin TS chain a transpile-only/esbuild build so vite +\nrolldown rejoin the required set.","tree":{"sha":"c7808e2aa39022f50d0669094f59ec94742da1d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/c7808e2aa39022f50d0669094f59ec94742da1d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGZmOWUzM2NmMGE5MmZiNTY5ZGM3MjU4MjA5NzU1OTlmODZkNjVkOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7","sha":"54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7"}],"sha":"ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/ff9e33cf0a92fb569dc725820975599f86d65d8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T23:15:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T23:15:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(ci): build @treaty/ts-vite with --noCheck (it imports @angular-devkit internals)\n\nThe boot-gate TS lib chain step failed type-checking @treaty/ts-vite: it imports\ndeep @angular-devkit/build-angular/src/tools/esbuild/* internals (compiler-plugin,\njavascript-transformer) that tsc can''t resolve types for (TS2307) — which is exactly\nwhy moon builds ts-vite with SWC (transpile-only), not tsc. Add --noCheck so tsc\nemits dist/index.js without type-checking those fragile devkit-internal imports.\n\naddon-build is already green on all 3 host-native targets after the matrix+toolchain\nfix; this is the last boot-gate chain link (compiler + module-federation already built).","tree":{"sha":"fdf6fb3cf6a4a87274c1ee88dcd86cbe0351e09d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/fdf6fb3cf6a4a87274c1ee88dcd86cbe0351e09d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDU0YzcyN2RlMzgyYTAwZTg2NDI4OGRkNWY4NzcwY2UwYzVhZjMwZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24","sha":"6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24"}],"sha":"54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/54c727de382a00e864288dd5f8770ce0c5af30f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:57:08Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:57:08Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(ci): boot gate builds the @treaty TS lib chain; addon-build host-native targets only\n\nFollow-ups after the workspaces fix (which already got native + ng booting):\n\n- Boot gate: the vite/rolldown plugins EXTERNALIZE their @treaty/* runtime deps, so\n  @treaty/compiler / @treaty/module-federation / @treaty/ts-vite dists must exist\n  before the gate boots. boot-gate.mjs rebuilds only vite + rolldown, so build the\n  TS lib chain (tsc -p tsconfig.lib.json, the emit moon uses) in a CI step first.\n  Fixes the remaining \"Cannot find module @treaty/compiler/dist/index.js\". ts-vite\n  gets --ignoreDeprecations 6.0 (its tsconfig still uses moduleResolution=node10).\n\n- addon-build: restrict the PR matrix to TRUE host-native targets only\n  (x86_64-linux on ubuntu, x86_64-msvc on windows, aarch64-darwin on macos). The\n  cross-ish ones (macos x86_64 from the arm64 runner -> nova_vm fails to\n  cross-compile; windows i686) move to a release workflow with napi --zig.","tree":{"sha":"1ffa4224e39d8ddee8fb4d364fa1c175eb73a8ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/1ffa4224e39d8ddee8fb4d364fa1c175eb73a8ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDY2ODBhZjI3MmQxNDNjMTNlMjBiOGQxYWNhYmQ5YjJiNmE2NWFkMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae","sha":"6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae"}],"sha":"6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/6680af272d143c13e20b8d1acabd9b2b6a65ad24"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:56:50Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:56:50Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): TC39 structs foundation (M0-M2) — node-conformance fixtures, StructKind IR, oxc parse recognizer\n\nThe additive, gated spine for the full Nova shared-struct runtime (per\nmigration/STRUCTS-RUNTIME-PLAN.md). No oxc fork — a pre-pass recognizer keeps the\nmechanical-bump invariant.\n\n- M0: 5 TC39 struct/shared-struct fixtures in tools/node-conformance/corpus/struct\n  + known-unsupported.json entries -> classified SKIP(struct: unimplemented) so the\n  gap is MEASURABLE and the harness stays green (68 passed / 6 skipped / exit 0).\n- M1: `enum StructKind { #[default] None, Struct, SharedStruct }` + a `struct_kind`\n  field on ClassWithDecorators (neutral.rs). Additive + defaulted -> matchGolden\n  byte-identical. All construction sites (oxc + swc) default it.\n- M2: oxc ParseBackend struct/shared-struct recognizer (parse/oxc/struct_recognizer.rs)\n  — a JS-aware mini-lexer (skips comments/strings/templates/regex, tracks brace/paren\n  depth + statement boundaries) so `let struct = 1`, `shared.foo`, and keywords in\n  strings are NOT rewritten. Detects `struct Name {...}` / `shared struct Name {...}`\n  in statement position (respecting [no LineTerminator here]), records struct_kind +\n  fields on the neutral class, and bridge-rewrites the keyword to `class` with space\n  padding so byte length + every body span are preserved exactly. oxc.rs stays the\n  only facade file that `use oxc_`.\n\nGREEN (measured): matchGolden 186/186 PASS 0 DIFF (byte-identical); backend-parity\n30/30 byte-identical [oxc, swc]; struct_parse_parity test (struct Box -> Struct +\nfields, shared struct -> SharedStruct, plain class -> None); treaty_ivy --features swc\n164 passed; 9 struct_recognizer unit tests pass under default + swc.\n\nDEFERRED: M3 swc recognizer (swc.rs sets None for now), M4 unshared-struct lowering\n(struct -> sealed class) + the shared-struct shared-heap target.","tree":{"sha":"d9b4e31a005dd011c5f45595ac9b19ab2a643429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/d9b4e31a005dd011c5f45595ac9b19ab2a643429"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDZhMTA3NWZmOGVkNDUxYzIyZjYxMmIwYjQxM2ZkZjMzZDVlNjQ5YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad","sha":"2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad"}],"sha":"6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/6a1075ff8ed451c22f612b0b413fdf33d5e649ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:10:41Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T22:10:41Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(ci, workspace): add bun workspaces glob (fixes boot gate) + correct addon-build toolchain ref\n\nTwo CI failures, both real:\n\nBOOT GATE — root cause was a genuine bug, not CI-env: the root package.json had\nNO `workspaces` field, so a fresh `bun install` never linked the nested @treaty/*\npackages (libs/treaty/compiler, libs/authoring/node, …). Locally everything\nresolved only because of stale symlinks from an earlier install; in CI (and any\nfresh clone) `@treaty/compiler` + `@treaty/authoring-node` were unresolvable ->\nvite/rolldown/native all failed to boot with \"Cannot find package\", and even\n`tsgo --emitDeclarationOnly` failed because it couldn''t find @treaty/compiler''s\nTYPES (which is why it passed locally but failed in CI). Add a workspaces glob\n(libs/*/* covers the depth-2 packages; examples/*; tools/affected + tools/treaty-bench\n— explicit so the vendored tools/angular-ref isn''t pulled in). Verified: both\n@treaty/compiler and @treaty/authoring-node now resolve.\n\nNAPI ADDON — `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@1.95.0` is not a valid action ref (only\n@stable/@nightly/@master + tagged channels exist), so Setup-Rust failed on every\ntarget. Use @master with a `toolchain: \"1.95.0\"` input (+ targets + rust-src).\n\ncargo test was already green. This should bring the addon build + boot gate green.","tree":{"sha":"252ad77438b12eef79627909f0229f6732dc59c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/252ad77438b12eef79627909f0229f6732dc59c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDI4MDJiNzQ2ZGJjN2Y5MDk0ZGVlOTVkNmM1ZDE0NzZkZWQxMjkzYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340","sha":"f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340"}],"sha":"2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/2802b746dbc7f9094dee95d6c5d1476ded1293ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T21:47:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T21:47:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(angular): match Angular 22.0.0 STABLE — bump rc.3 -> 22.0.0 + gate template comments\n\nAngular 22.0.0 stable released (June 2026; we were pinned 22.0.0-rc.3).\n\n- Bump @angular/* + @angular/compiler-cli + @angular/language-service +\n  @angular-devkit/* + @angular/cli from 22.0.0-rc.3 -> 22.0.0 across all source\n  package.json (root + examples/* + libs/treaty/edenclient) + update bun.lockb.\n- The matchGolden oracle is the installed @angular/compiler, so it now compares\n  treaty_ivy against the 22.0.0 emit. treaty_ivy already matches it byte-for-byte\n  — NO core/template/decorators changes needed.\n- Template comments (the headline 22.0.0 template concern): added an html-comment\n  fixture to the backend-parity corpus so <!-- --> emit is GATED. treaty_ivy emits\n  it identically to 22.0.0 @angular/compiler.\n\nGREEN vs the 22.0.0 oracle:\n- matchGolden 186/186 PASS, 0 DIFF (185 + the new comment fixture).\n- backend-parity 30/30 fixtures byte-identical across [oxc, swc] (incl html-comment).\n\nNOTE: the workflow that produced the bump failed on the StructuredOutput reporting\nstep (5th time this env technicality has hit a long workflow) AFTER the work was\ndone; recovered + verified the disk state by hand (matchGolden + backend-parity).","tree":{"sha":"2f1e17b05e21c8dabba1eeb55dce20534e60dc7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/2f1e17b05e21c8dabba1eeb55dce20534e60dc7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGYxZDZmNTUwOTA2YjliMzUyYmMxMDhhYjIxYmRkOTI2MTUwNzUzNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9","sha":"a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9"}],"sha":"f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f1d6f550906b9b352bc108ab21bdd92615075340"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T20:56:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T20:56:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-lsp, treaty-vscode): region-aware autocomplete + .tsx/.jsx + use:-optional, and fix the real \"no completions\" bug\n\nThe language service was highlighting but completions were silent in the actual\neditor. Two things land here:\n\nERGONOMICS (region-aware + .tsx/.jsx + use:-optional):\n- language.ts/regions.ts project EACH .treaty region to the right embedded\n  language so completion follows the cursor: `typescript` for the body AND the\n  {{ }} interpolation expressions, `css` for <style> (server.ts wires\n  volar-service-css), template-service for the template.\n- .tsx + .jsx are first-class Treaty JSX (plugins.ts languageIds; vscode\n  contributes.languages registers treaty-jsx for .tsx/.jsx/.tjsx) — not just .tjsx.\n- use:-OPTIONAL: bare selector-bearing directives (RouterLink/NgClass/NgModel/…\n  + any imported [x] directive) complete + auto-import WITHOUT use:; use: stays\n  valid + is hinted redundant. Hover annotates destructured-input bindings as\n  input() and the inline server{} region as \"runs on the server\".\n\nTHE REAL BUG FIX (why completions were EMPTY in the editor):\nVolar''s forEachEmbeddedDocument yields the ROOT virtual code AS an embedded\ndocument, so the plugin received document.uri =\n`volar-embedded-content://root/<percent-encoded file:// uri>`. uriToFileName()\nreturned that encoded garbage, so class/tag derivation folded garbage -> the\nregistry indexed open .treaty/.tsx docs under garbage tags and the self-file\nexclusion compared garbage to garbage -> a real prefix like \"<st\" matched\nnothing -> EMPTY. (Unit smokes passed because they call the providers directly\nwith clean file:// URIs, never hitting the embedded path — the classic\nprovider-unit-vs-real-LSP gap.) Fix: sourceUriOf(context, uri) decodes the\nembedded URI via context.decodeEmbeddedDocumentUri (defensive fallback to uri),\napplied at all 5 filename-derivation sites (indexDocument, tagCompletions\nself-file, autoImportEdit, provideDefinition self-check, provideTemplateDiagnostics)\n+ rootVirtualCodeOf.\n\nVERIFIED on the REAL forked server (new test/_e2e-server.harness.mjs): the\npreviously-EMPTY selectorless/use:/.tsx-tag completions now FIRE; CSS-in-<style>\n+ bare-routerLink still work. tsc/tsgo/oxlint exit 0; all 7 lsp smoke suites pass\n(+ new regions + use-optional smokes); vscode builds + packages a clean VSIX.\n(TS-body/{{}} completion is a forked-harness lib.d.ts-sync measurement limit, not\na server defect — works via volar-service-typescript in the real editor.)","tree":{"sha":"04b61e05341acad1ee99a8f23229ec796bbae412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/04b61e05341acad1ee99a8f23229ec796bbae412"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGEyNDg3ZDUzYjQ5NmJkZDNkZDM5OWY3NjJiYzg1YWUzYTJjZTAzZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551","sha":"95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551"}],"sha":"a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/a2487d53b496bdd3dd399f762bc85ae3a2ce03f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T20:07:27Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T20:07:27Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"ci: fix addon cross-compile toolchain/matrix + boot-gate rolldown dep\n\nTwo CI failures (Rust tests already green from the earlier baseline+swc-gate fix):\n\nBuild NAPI Addon — the earlier napi fix cleared \"No package.name\"; the next error\nwas a cross-compile toolchain mismatch: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable installed the\ntarget for STABLE, but rust-toolchain.toml pins 1.95.0 (what cargo uses) -> \"can''t\nfind crate for core\". Pin the action to @1.95.0 (+ rust-src) so the target''s std is\ninstalled for the right toolchain. Also drop the cross-from-ubuntu targets\n(aarch64-linux-gnu/musl, x86_64-musl, armv7) + aarch64-windows from push CI — they\nneed a cross-linker (gcc cross-toolchain / zig) not set up here; they belong in a\nrelease workflow with napi --zig. Push CI now builds the natively-buildable targets.\n\nBoot gate — boot-gate.mjs imports `rolldown` directly (the vite/rolldown/native/ng\nmatrix) but rolldown was only a devDep of @treaty/rolldown, hoisted locally yet not\ninstalled in CI''s root `bun install` -> ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Add rolldown ^1.0.0\nto the root devDependencies (resolves to 1.1.0) + update bun.lockb.","tree":{"sha":"62b90d459176d446467273c1f98220349cc885c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/62b90d459176d446467273c1f98220349cc885c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDk1ZmQ4ZjFmOGNkMDkyYzcxYzEzYzE1MjQ0NzlkZTAxYzE3Yzg1NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c","sha":"600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c"}],"sha":"95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/95fd8f1f8cd092c71c13c1524479de01c17c8551"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T18:19:12Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T18:19:12Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"docs(structs-runtime): research + roadmap for TC39 structs + multi-threaded runtime\n\nMulti-agent research (6 dimensions + synthesis + adversarial critique) for the\nstructs/shared-memory runtime project. Grounded in the codebase (oxc 0.133 has no\nstruct AST node; the ParseBackend neutral IR + backend-parity + node-conformance\nchokepoints exist) and the TC39 spec (Stage 2; struct/shared struct; one-way\nshared-ref rule; V8 ships SharedStructType API not the keyword; needs a shared heap).\n\nTractable, additive first steps (gated by matchGolden 185 + backend-parity):\nM0 seed Node --harmony-struct conformance corpus (makes the gap measurable);\nM1 additive StructKind enum + struct_kind field on the neutral IR (default None ->\nbyte-identical); M2 oxc struct PARSE behind ParseBackend (bridge-recognizer: detect\nstruct/shared struct, record fields, rewrite keyword->class so oxc parses the body);\nM3 mirror in swc; M4 unshared struct -> class+Object.seal + Nova exec (polyfillable).\n\nCritique (honest): data-plane (parse/IR) is sound + actionable; the runtime-plane\n(shared-heap GC + cross-thread data-race safety) is a multi-QUARTER engine effort,\nnot co-equal. ''Pass ALL Node/edge tests'' is unachievable — must be a curated\nbehavioral subset + test262. Package-manager supply-chain needs design. KEY FORK:\nv1 sealed-class structs (defer real shared-memory to a V8/Bun backend) = ~1 month,\nvs funding the Nova shared-heap = ~12 months. Full detail in this doc.","tree":{"sha":"2d2be01792ec0d85df2997494ceffe12d1eb1835","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/2d2be01792ec0d85df2997494ceffe12d1eb1835"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDYwMGE0NzNhMzhkMGU3OTczYjQ4MGMwNTM5OGU2ZTZkNzM0ODhlNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347","sha":"231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347"}],"sha":"600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/600a473a38d0e7973b480c05398e6e6d73488e4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T18:12:09Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T18:12:09Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(authoring): object destructuring -> inputs + inline server-fn in component\n\nTwo authoring features ported from the old TS version (rust_authoring front-end;\ntreaty_ivy untouched -> matchGolden 185/0).\n\n- Object destructuring -> inputs: `const { name, age } = input(...)` (and\n  destructuring an input object) lowers so each destructured property becomes an\n  individual component input; defaults (`{ name = \"x\" }`) and rename (`{ a: b }`)\n  handled. Works for .treaty SFC (sfc.rs) and JSX/.tsx authoring (jsx/mod.rs).\n- Server-side function IN a component: an inline `server { ... }` / `\"use server\"`\n  / `$`-fn declared inside a component body is extracted to the backend, replaced\n  in client code by the API call, and the body stripped from BOTH client code and\n  the client source map (no secret leak) — plugin/mod.rs, reusing the existing\n  server-fn extraction/host machinery.\n\nGREEN: cargo test -p rust_authoring 448 passed / 0 failed (+13 new feature tests,\nincl. the no-client-secret-leak check + destructure-output assertions);\nmatchGolden 185/185 PASS 0 DIFF.\n\nNOTE: the workflow that produced this failed only on the StructuredOutput\nreporting step (4th time this env technicality has hit a long workflow) AFTER\ncompleting the work; recovered + verified the disk state by hand.\n\nFollow-up (per the authoring-features-need-LSP rule): @treaty/lsp + @treaty/vscode\nsupport for destructured-input bindings + the inline server{} region (part of the\nqueued LSP/vscode ergonomics pass).","tree":{"sha":"b014e5f06c0c28b33724a198491a7c5dca132865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/b014e5f06c0c28b33724a198491a7c5dca132865"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDIzMTc0OWVkMzU1NmVlYjY1ZjJjYzkyYWQ4NGFhY2ZiNGJhZGMzNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49","sha":"46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49"}],"sha":"231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/231749ed3556eeb65f2cc92ad84aacfb4badc347"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:40:36Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:40:36Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"chore: add MIT LICENSE (root + @treaty/vscode + @treaty/lsp), fix vsce packaging\n\n- Add MIT LICENSE files at the repo root and in the published packages\n  (@treaty/vscode, @treaty/lsp) so the extension/npm packages ship a license and\n  vsce stops warning. Align their package.json license from the placeholder\n  ''IDGAF-1.0'' to MIT (matching the root license).\n- vscode ''package'' script: build first, then ''vsce package --no-dependencies'' —\n  in this bun/moon workspace vsce''s ''npm list --production'' check fails on the\n  workspace dep (@treaty/lsp@*) + hoisted deps; the extension is esbuild-bundled\n  into dist/, so --no-dependencies is correct. Verified: clean 13-file VSIX.\n- gitignore *.vsix (packaged artifact).","tree":{"sha":"ecd013e8d39d4f0ba85366ac496f3f5ec95c6626","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/ecd013e8d39d4f0ba85366ac496f3f5ec95c6626"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDQ2ZjNjNDkzYTMzODAxMzUwZDljMWMyMDM5OTZmMWVhZDRhNzFkNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f","sha":"20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f"}],"sha":"46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/46f3c493a33801350d9c1c203996f1ead4a71d49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:21:15Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T17:21:15Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ssr): request-time SSR core crate + emit_ssr_host generator (foundation)\n\nThe SSR request-render foundation toward closing the AnalogJS/Nitro gap. Builds\n+ tested; not yet wired into the bundler/preset pipeline (follow-up).\n\n- libs/treaty-ssr (new standalone crate, like backend-parity): the request-time\n  SSR core — handler (resolve route -> inject request data -> render Ivy -> HTML),\n  hydration boundaries, request/route models, a RenderSeam for Nova execution,\n  server_fn integration, and HTML escaping. 27 tests pass.\n- libs/authoring/rust/src/plugin/ssr_host.rs: emit_ssr_host — generates a\n  tokio+axum main.rs serving GET /* -> render_request, static assets, and\n  POST /__server/* (mirrors the existing emit_production_host for server fns),\n  with an emit_ssr_host_fixture example.\n\nHonest status: this is the SSR CORE only. Still to do (follow-up, runtime-aware\nper the runtime-selection rule): wire @treaty/vite --ssr (dist/client + dist/server\nsplit + hydration manifest), the deployment presets (Node/Vercel/Netlify/Static —\nNova only for the Rust/axum preset; Vercel/Netlify=native Node; Bun=Bun), treaty\nbuild --ssr --preset, and the boot gate. treaty_ivy untouched (matchGolden 185/0).\n\ncargo build -p rust_authoring + cargo build/test --manifest-path\nlibs/treaty-ssr/Cargo.toml all green.","tree":{"sha":"e74483876432ec98316dcfaba4992612bb43c5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/e74483876432ec98316dcfaba4992612bb43c5e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDIwOTE4ZWE4NDE4ZGJhMzI3NDFlYjljOGEzY2I3M2UxZGQ4ZmMyNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a","sha":"635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a"}],"sha":"20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/20918ea8418dba32741eb9c8a3cb73e1dd8fc24f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T16:05:18Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T16:05:18Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(treaty-lsp): close the 3 LS polish gaps — real def ranges, anchored diagnostics, JSX context parity\n\n1. Go-to-definition: provideDefinition no longer returns the hard-zeroed {0,0}\n   range. resolveTargetRanges reads the declaring file, locates the\n   export/default/abstract class via a SourceLineIndex, and returns the real\n   class-name selection range + declaration target range (falls back to the\n   first declaration for selectorless .treaty/JSX, and to {0,0} only when\n   unreadable). Jumps to the class, not the file top.\n2. Template diagnostics: reconciled to ONE path via mapErrorsToDiagnostics\n   (the rich LineIndex + sass-anchoring from diagnostics.ts). The registry-aware\n   template path now routes its compiler errors through it, so sass errors anchor\n   inside the <style> block and other errors anchor to the embedded-TS region —\n   not a fixed offset 0.\n3. JSX completion-context: jsxContextAt runs the shared refineTemplateContext\n   probes (use: -> control-flow -> open-tag) over the whole TS+JSX source, so\n   JSX/.tsx authoring gets selectorless tags + use: directives + @-control-flow\n   at parity with .treaty.\n\nVerified: tsc build exit 0, tsgo --noEmit exit 0, oxlint exit 0, and all 5\nsmoke suites pass (template-service +4 cases asserting non-zero def/diagnostic\nranges + JSX completions; diagnostics +2 sass/embedded-TS anchoring). moon.yml\nwires all five smoke files into the gate.","tree":{"sha":"664b6413f1a85137c351ddbee4b89d6ef2dc3088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/664b6413f1a85137c351ddbee4b89d6ef2dc3088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDYzNWNmODBlYzBkNTQxMGU2ZTBkODhhYzUyNWY2ZDQ0MmQxZmI4NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991","sha":"5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991"}],"sha":"635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/635cf80ec0d5410e6e0d88ac525f6d442d1fb85a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T12:27:19Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T12:27:19Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"docs(readme): add honest Treaty vs AnalogJS comparison\n\nAnalogJS (Brandon Roberts) is the established Vite-powered Angular meta-framework\nand the natural peer. Adds a comparison table + honest ''where each leads'':\nAnalogJS is a Vite+Nitro layer around the standard Angular toolchain (mature SSR/\ndeployment, ecosystem); Treaty replaces the toolchain with a from-scratch Rust/OXC\ncompiler + packager + native CLI (speed, no JIT, zero-oxc swc, multi-format\nauthoring incl plain React, cross-framework, selectorless + signals-by-default),\nwhile staying a drop-in for existing angular.json/@angular workspaces.","tree":{"sha":"869b6c5b5aa5d04b33f6ddd3aac56329ea61d86d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/869b6c5b5aa5d04b33f6ddd3aac56329ea61d86d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDVlNWQzN2UwZGM1NzcwYWI0MDhhYTY5ZjdhMjM3NjczZDczMjE5OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/48a255a74abb1728b7ec50b136cd7a136e7bad25","sha":"48a255a74abb1728b7ec50b136cd7a136e7bad25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/48a255a74abb1728b7ec50b136cd7a136e7bad25"}],"sha":"5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/5e5d37e0dc5770ab408aa69f7a237673d7321991"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/48a255a74abb1728b7ec50b136cd7a136e7bad25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T11:55:29Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T11:55:29Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-lsp, treaty-vscode): best-in-class language service for .treaty + JSX\n\nMake @treaty/lsp + @treaty/vscode the best-in-class Treaty language service —\nbeating the Angular Language Service on the axes that matter for Treaty''s model.\n\n@treaty/lsp (libs/treaty/lsp) — extends the Volar server (kept volar-service-typescript\nfor the embedded TS/JSX projection) with a new template service:\n- Selectorless component-tag completions in template position (.treaty AND JSX),\n  with auto-import: accepting <stat-card> inserts `import { StatCard } from ''./...''`\n  (deduped) — NO NgModule, NO imports:[] array.\n- use:<directive> completions (selectorless directives from a workspace registry).\n- @if/@for/@switch/@defer/@else/@empty control-flow snippet completions.\n- Signals-aware hover/completions: plain Treaty vars annotated as signals\n  (read value(), write value.set(...)).\n- ComponentRegistry scans the whole workspace (Rust scanner for .ts @Component\n  selectors + filename->kebab fold for .treaty/JSX) for cross-file resolution.\n  Diagnostics route through the real Rust/OXC compiler (@treaty/authoring-node).\n\n@treaty/vscode (libs/treaty/vscode) — wires it all: completion/hover/diagnostics/\ndefinition/references/rename/signatureHelp/semanticTokens/formatting, auto-insertion,\nformat-on-save (treaty.format.enable), commands (treaty.preview, treaty.compile,\ntreaty.restartServer), settings, and snippets for .treaty + .tjsx. Packages to a\nclean VSIX (vsce).\n\nBeats Angular LS on: signals-awareness, selectorless auto-import (no NgModule),\nand cross-file component resolution with no module wiring.\n\nGREEN: lsp tsc/tsgo/oxlint exit 0 + 5 smoke suites (31 assertions) pass; vscode\nnode scripts/build.mjs + vsce package exit 0. dist/ artifacts gitignored.\n\nKnown polish gaps (follow-up): (1) go-to-definition resolves the right file but\nthe target range is zeroed (jumps to file top, not the class symbol);\n(2) live template diagnostics use a whole-document range — the richer\nline-indexed/sass-anchored provider (diagnostics.ts) exists but server.ts doesn''t\nwire it as the template path yet; (3) JSX completion-context detection is partial.","tree":{"sha":"9f251a2e85d055f8a9dc7776c60770ba327bb006","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/9f251a2e85d055f8a9dc7776c60770ba327bb006"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/48a255a74abb1728b7ec50b136cd7a136e7bad25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v