drift is CLEAN again. backend-parity parity (oxc vs swc) stays 29/29.","tree":{"sha":"5c5873e484b06d4a91523e71003c9b7ed24f2db9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/5c5873e484b06d4a91523e71003c9b7ed24f2db9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/9c14fcd2545aa163eca418ba8b0bdd2f6c036fc1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/9c14fcd2545aa163eca418ba8b0bdd2f6c036fc1","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDljMTRmY2QyNTQ1YWExNjNlY2E0MThiYThiMGJkZDJmNmMwMzZmYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c","sha":"ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c"}],"sha":"9c14fcd2545aa163eca418ba8b0bdd2f6c036fc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/9c14fcd2545aa163eca418ba8b0bdd2f6c036fc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T09:55:44Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T09:55:44Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): TRUE ZERO-OXC swc backend — swc compiles the whole corpus byte-identically, no oxc linked\n\nCompletes the zero-oxc wide port (steps 1+2 in c7efaf2, 9ce8234). The last\noxc stronghold — source_compile.rs''s ~3700-line AOT walk — is now neutral, so\n`--features swc` links ZERO oxc and swc compiles every fixture byte-for-byte\nidentically to oxc. oxc stays the default/preferred backend.\n\nIR extension (core/src/neutral.rs): added the ctor-param TYPE-TOKEN surface\n(constructor DI token from `param: Type`) + the fn RETURN-TYPE surface\n(ModuleWithProviders<T> etc.) — the last two things the AOT source front-end\nread from live oxc types. Both backends fill them byte-identically (parse_parity).\n\nWalk ported off oxc (facade):\n- source_compile.rs: compile_program_with_source + its ~280 oxc references now\n  consume the neutral ParseOutput (classes w/ spans + members + ctor-param types,\n  top_level, nprops, fn-return-type) instead of &oxc_ast::Program. OxcLive /\n  ClassMeta::live deleted; byte-exact strip/emit ranges come from neutral\n  TreatySpan + ParseBackend::span_text.\n- partial_class_metadata.rs: ported to the neutral surface.\n- parse/oxc.rs (OxcParseBackend) gated behind #[cfg(feature=\"oxc\")]; facade oxc_*\n  deps optional + `oxc` feature; the ParsingBackend alias is SwcParseBackend under\n  `swc`. emitter_swc.rs finalized as the swc emit path.\n\nPROVEN (measured):\n- cargo tree -p treaty_ivy --no-default-features --features swc => 0 oxc_* crates.\n- matchGolden on the DEFAULT (oxc) build: 185/185, 0 DIFF.\n- matchGolden on the SWC build: 185/185, 0 DIFF — and the oxc vs swc corpus dumps\n  are BYTE-IDENTICAL (diff clean).\n- backend-parity 29/29 [oxc,swc]; parse_parity real-corpus 1225/0 (10 tests).\n- treaty_ivy tests: 144+12 (default oxc) / 144 (swc), 0 failed. packagr + CLI\n  build green on default features.\n\nNet: Treaty now has two interchangeable, byte-identical compiler backends — oxc\n(default/preferred) and a fully native, zero-oxc swc — selectable by cargo\nfeature. oxc is confined behind the ParseBackend trait (parse/oxc.rs), so future\noxc bumps touch only that surface.","tree":{"sha":"08af71ee49130ba5ec795ec7d6fa514d2edda3ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/08af71ee49130ba5ec795ec7d6fa514d2edda3ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGFiNmZmNWMzZTBlNzM4OTBmYWZlY2RlNWQ4ZGVhMmZkYmM1MDc1N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638","sha":"9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638"}],"sha":"ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/ab6ff5c3e0e73890fafecde5d8dea2fdbc50757c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T19:10:22Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T19:10:22Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"refactor(treaty-ivy): zero-oxc step 2 — partial_emit + linker + core + template off oxc; IR spans/top-level/nprops\n\nContinues the zero-oxc port (oxc still default + byte-identical). Three more\noxc strongholds neutralized; only the source_compile AOT walk remains.\n\nIR extension (core/src/neutral.rs) — closes the 3 gaps the prior run flagged:\n- TreatySpan on ClassWithDecorators (+ stmt_span), DecoratorInfo, MemberInfo —\n  carries the load-bearing strip/emit ranges (class.span.start forward-ref\n  Closure, recognized_decorator_strip_span, decorated_stmt_start).\n- NTopStmt/NAssignment + ParseOutput::top_level (source order) — the neutral\n  top-level surface for partial_emit::collect_rewrites (X.ɵfac=/X.ɵprov=\n  ɵɵdefineInjectable assignments, ɵɵsetNgModuleScope, factory-body decompile);\n  NArg + NObjectProp::KeyValue gain byte spans for token slices.\n- ObjLit::nprops (full NExpr per property) — lossless ngDeclare/decorator object\n  values (providers, useFactory arrows, transform fns) for the linker walk.\nBoth OxcParseBackend and SwcParseBackend populate every new field byte-identically\n(reconciled 2 cross-engine span quirks: abstract-class decorator anchoring).\n\nWalk switched off oxc (facade):\n- partial_emit.rs walks ParseOutput::top_level + span_text — zero use oxc_,\n  factory-body decompile is now a structural NExpr/NStmt walk.\n- linker.rs drives link_*/convert_expr off ObjLit::nprops + NExpr and consumes\n  ng_declare_calls directly (NgDeclareCall.call_span; no per-decl re-parse) —\n  zero use oxc_.\n\ncore + template oxc-free under swc:\n- core: 4 oxc_* deps now optional + `oxc` feature; the oxc Lowerer + all oxc\n  imports #[cfg]-gated behind oxc (emitter_swc is the swc emit path). Builds\n  --no-default-features --features swc with ZERO oxc.\n- template/facade Cargo: oxc/swc feature pass-through, default-features=false.\n\nMEASURED byte-identical: matchGolden 185/185 PASS / 0 DIFF (dump identical to\nbaseline). backend-parity 29/29 [oxc,swc]. parse_parity 1225/0 (+ partial-AOT\ncorpus). Suites: core 215, template 62, decorators 153, facade 144+12. core +\ntemplate build swc-only with zero oxc.\n\nRemaining (step 3): extend IR with ctor-param type annotations + fn return-type,\nport source_compile.rs compile_program_with_source (~3700-line AOT walk) +\npartial_class_metadata.rs off live oxc, gate parse/oxc.rs behind `oxc`, flip the\nswc alias → true zero-oxc + swc-build matchGolden 185/185.","tree":{"sha":"b8865462cd424ecaaa61b16379ac1e17bd95f943","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/b8865462cd424ecaaa61b16379ac1e17bd95f943"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDljZTgyMzQzZWYzMTFjNGIzNzQ2NzVmZTk0Y2E2NDI4NmM2NmQ2Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4","sha":"c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4"}],"sha":"9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/9ce82343ef311c4b374675fe94ca64286c66d638"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T17:35:57Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T17:35:57Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"refactor(treaty-ivy): zero-oxc step 1/2 — full neutral IR in core + oxc-free decorators crate\n\nToward a true zero-oxc swc variant: neutralize the compiler''s public surface\noff live oxc AST nodes onto an engine-neutral IR (byte-identical, oxc still default).\n\n- treaty_ivy_core::neutral (NEW): the engine-neutral IR moved here as pure owned\n  data (no oxc types) so every crate can name it — ObjLit/LitValue/TreatySpan +\n  the full NExpr (all 18 Expression variants incl arrow/function bodies; binary\n  and logical unified into Binary{op} keyed by source spelling) / NStmt /\n  NCtorParam / NParam / NVarDeclarator / NArrayElement / NObjectProp / NArg /\n  ImportInfo / MemberKind, plus DecoratorInfo (full neutral arguments) /\n  MemberInfo (kind/static/params/initializer) / ClassWithDecorators. facade\n  parse/mod.rs re-exports them from their historical crate::parse::* paths.\n- treaty_ivy_decorators: ClassMeta now carries the neutral\n  ClassWithDecorators/DecoratorInfo/ObjLit plus an OPAQUE caller-defined\n  `live: &L` handle the crate never inspects; ClassMeta/DecoratorCompiler/\n  DecoratorRegistry are generic over L. The oxc_ast import AND dependency are\n  REMOVED — the decorators crate now links zero oxc and names no oxc type.\n- facade: a facade-private OxcLive<''a> threads the live &Class/&ObjectExpression\n  through ClassMeta::live so the transitional metadata walk stays byte-identical\n  while the decorator API is fully neutral. Both OxcParseBackend and\n  SwcParseBackend populate the extended IR in SOURCE order; fixed two cross-engine\n  shape diffs the parity sweep surfaced (rest params, shorthand object props).\n\nMEASURED, byte-identical: matchGolden 185/185 PASS / 0 DIFF (dump byte-for-byte\nidentical to baseline, 921132 bytes). backend-parity 29/29 [oxc,swc].\nparse_parity 1225/1225 over the real Angular corpus. Suites green: core 215,\ndecorators 62, facade 144 (default) / 151 (--features swc), real-packages 12.\n\nRemaining for zero-oxc (step 2/2): extend the neutral IR with spans on\nclass/decorator/member nodes + a top-level assignment surface (for\npartial_emit::collect_rewrites) + full NExpr in ngDeclare object values, then\nswitch the facade/linker/partial_emit walk + core/template off live oxc and\nfeature-gate oxc so --features swc links none.","tree":{"sha":"a00f6b659558a6910930652e7fe69436ad4b55e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/a00f6b659558a6910930652e7fe69436ad4b55e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGM3ZWZhZjJjMTA2OTRiZGQxYmFjYjdkZDZmNDllZTU0ZDA5NzQ3YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324","sha":"036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324"}],"sha":"c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/c7efaf2c10694bdd1bacb7dd6f49ee54d09747a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T16:45:33Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T16:45:33Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"docs(readme): refresh for 185/185, dual oxc/swc backend, treaty-packagr ng-packagr byte-parity, native ng-compatible CLI, cross-module selectors, rolldown plugin, modernizer, benchmark suite","tree":{"sha":"757b5b584ae7dc5b402fd6fedb4594a59f386e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/757b5b584ae7dc5b402fd6fedb4594a59f386e2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDAzNmMxYTU2ZTY4M2Y4Zjg1ZjY3ODM1NjMwNmVkODc5ZTdiMmYzMjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3","sha":"7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3"}],"sha":"036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/036c1a56e683f8f85f678356306ed879e7b2f324"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T16:33:32Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T16:33:32Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): SWC parse backend — ParseBackend trait + byte-identical SwcParseBackend (oxc preferred)\n\nApproach-B parse-seam abstraction so treaty_ivy can parse Angular/TS source\nwith EITHER oxc (default/preferred) or swc, gated byte-identical.\n\nparse/mod.rs — ParseBackend trait (parse_module via owned-arena callback +\nspan_text) + engine-neutral ParseOutput / ClassWithDecorators / DecoratorInfo /\nMemberInfo / ObjLit / LitValue (String/Number/Boolean/Null/Identifier/Array/\nObject + Other(span) so nothing is silently dropped) / NgDeclareCall / TreatySpan\n/ SourceKind. Feature-gated ParsingBackend alias (oxc default). Mirrors the emit\nchokepoint precedent.\n\nparse/oxc.rs — OxcParseBackend: the ONLY facade file constructing a parser\n(Parser::new / Allocator / SourceType now confined here). Fills the neutral\nstructs in SOURCE order (faithful to the historical key_name/decorator_object/\nstring_value helpers) and exposes the live Program for the byte-identity walk.\n\nparse/swc.rs — SwcParseBackend: parses with swc_ecma_parser inside its own\nGLOBALS+SourceMap (no shared thread-local; rayon/compileMany safe), walks\nswc_ecma_ast to fill the SAME neutral structs in source order. span_text rebases\nswc BytePos to absolute offsets. swc deps (swc_common 16 / swc_ecma_ast 17 /\nswc_ecma_parser 26 / swc_atoms 8) are optional + swc-feature-gated, off by default.\n\nAll 9 parse call sites (source_compile x5, linker, partial_emit) migrated to\nParsingBackend::default().parse_module(src, kind, |module| { ... }).\n\nMEASURED, byte-identical:\n- cargo build -p treaty_ivy default + --no-default-features --features swc: GREEN.\n- cargo test -p treaty_ivy: 156 pass / 0 fail (default); 162 / 0 (--features swc,\n  incl 6 parse_parity tests).\n- PARSE parity (new parse_parity_real_corpus): swc''s neutral ParseOutput ==\n  oxc''s across ALL 1225 .ts files of the real Angular compliance corpus — 1225 OK\n  / 0 DIFF (fixed 16->0 genuine DIFFs: swc method-decorator placement, constructor\n  naming, computed string keys, stray `;` members).\n- backend-parity (oxc,swc): 29/29 byte-identical.\n- matchGolden on default build: 185/185, dump proven byte-identical to baseline.\n\nSCOPE / follow-up (honest): the parse SEAM is abstracted, but the downstream\nAOT/linker WALK (compile_program_with_source(&Program), collect_rewrites,\nlink_partial_walk, and the treaty_ivy_decorators ClassMeta API) still consumes\nthe live oxc AST, so `cargo tree --features swc` still links oxc. True zero-oxc\n(SWC-BACKEND-PLAN §3.2 Phase-3 wide port) requires neutralizing that walk across\nall 4 crates + feature-gating oxc — a separate effort tracked next. swc is wired\n+ gated via the parity test, not yet the runtime alias.","tree":{"sha":"7abb8ccf7a4ebf1ac3042e3583598b4bb930ded1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/7abb8ccf7a4ebf1ac3042e3583598b4bb930ded1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDdlNTdmOWUyZTI0MDQyMDJmOGZmMjgwOTUyZWQ3ZWIxNzdlYmM1ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2","sha":"eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2"}],"sha":"7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/7e57f9e2e2404202f8ff280952ed7eb177ebc5e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T15:43:16Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T15:43:16Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-packagr): ng-packagr byte-parity — classic-@Input .d.ts, real version stamp, FESM-faithful CSS optimizer\n\nFinalize treaty-packagr against a real ng-packagr@21.2.3 (@angular/core\n22.0.0-rc.3) build as the SOLE oracle:\n\n.d.ts (component_dts.rs)\n- Omit `isSignal` for a classic `@Input` (ngc emits it only when true), and\n  terminate every input-map entry with a trailing `;` before the closing brace\n  (`{ \"name\": { ... }; }`) — closing the last byte so the emitted ɵcmp .d.ts is\n  byte-identical to ng-packagr. Classic-input tests updated to expect the key\n  OMITTED + a regression test locks the trailing-`;` inputs-map form.\n\npartial version (library.rs)\n- stamp_partial_version rewrites the treaty_ivy `0.0.0-PLACEHOLDER` sentinel to\n  the lib''s real package.json version across every ɵɵngDeclare* form + the\n  partial ɵsetClassMetadata.\n\nCSS optimizer (css_optimizer.rs) — FESM is the oracle, NOT esbuild\n- Corrects the prior (wrong) \"matches esbuild\" claim: ng-packagr''s emitted FESM\n  `styles` bytes are the ground truth. ng-packagr order is\n  encapsulateStyle(esbuildBundleFile(css)) — esbuild minifies pre-scope, then\n  ngc ShadowCss scopes; treaty''s order is the reverse (ShadowCss then this\n  optimizer post-pass). So this optimizer reproduces exactly the esbuild\n  transforms that SURVIVE ShadowCss while NOT re-doing what ShadowCss already\n  normalized:\n    * KEEP the selector-list `, ` (comma+space) and combinators ` > ` ` + ` ` ~ `\n      that ShadowCss re-emits — do not tighten them;\n    * TIGHTEN the `@media (min-width: 600px)` → `@media(min-width:600px)` prelude\n      (the FESM is tighter here than even ng-packagr''s own esbuild stage);\n    * keyframe `from`→`0%`, zero-angle `rotate(0deg)`→`rotate(0)`,\n      attribute-selector quote strip, `::before`→`:before`, `!important` tighten;\n    * leave custom-property (`--x`) values verbatim (ng-packagr does not minify).\n  Every expectation is annotated with the captured ng-packagr bytes it\n  reproduces (oracle captured from a real ng-packagr@21 build).\n\nLess/Stylus stay an honest surveyed passthrough (no pure-Rust engine exists);\ndocs/diagnostics improved to name the language + state that.\n\ncargo test -p treaty_packagr GREEN: 76 tests, 0 failed (incl. the\nscoped_fixture_is_byte_identical_to_ng_packagr_fesm integration test + the\nng_byte_* regression tests asserting the captured ng-packagr FESM bytes). The\npackagr bench (results/packagr.json, REPORT.md) refreshed: ivyAllEqual +\ndtsAllEqual true. A live real-ng-packagr re-diff will re-confirm in the\nbenchmark capstone on final binaries.","tree":{"sha":"286e960fa2b7866b3a3aac3c7e70d57848806140","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/286e960fa2b7866b3a3aac3c7e70d57848806140"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGViOTMzMWQxMDYwYzE3MDQ5NTQ0NmI1NmQ4ZDJiNmQ0NThkMTk3YjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6","sha":"22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6"}],"sha":"eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/eb9331d1060c170495446b56d8d2b6d458d197b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T10:20:43Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T10:20:43Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-cli): 1:1 Angular-CLI compat — angular.json architects + real @angular-devkit schematics/migrations\n\nMake the native `treaty` CLI a drop-in for `ng`:\n\n- angular.rs: parse angular.json (workspace + projects + each architect\n  target: builder/options/per-config overrides/defaultConfiguration +\n  per-project schematics defaults). resolve_architect_target merges base\n  options with the selected/default configuration and projects\n  outputPath/browser|main/index/tsConfig/styles/assets to absolute paths.\n  find_angular_json walks up; config.rs prefers angular.json, falls back\n  to treaty.config.json/conventions.\n- `treaty build`/`serve --project <p> -c <config>` resolve the architect\n  target and run through Treaty (native Rust module-graph build / tokio\n  serve). Verified: `treaty build` in examples/ng-bench-app resolves\n  build:production (@angular/build:application), emits 268 modules, and the\n  dist headless-boots JIT-free (works=PASS, Dashboard rendered).\n- `treaty generate`/`new`/`update`/`test`/`lint` spawn the genuine\n  @angular-devkit (NodeWorkflow) + @schematics/angular / real architect\n  builders via Node (node_cmd.rs + src/js/run-schematic.mjs +\n  run-migration.mjs) — args passed straight through, truly 1:1. Verified\n  generate creates real files with the project prefix; update runs the\n  real migration NodeWorkflow.\n\nHonest divergence: `treaty build` runs Treaty''s own native build, not\n@angular/build:application''s optimizer — output is a correct JIT-free\nbootable Angular dist, not yet byte-for-byte optimized ng output (a\nsurfaced follow-up; --bundler rolldown for optimized output).\n\ncargo build -p treaty_cli + full workspace GREEN; cargo test -p treaty_cli\n86 passed / 0 failed (incl. real-devkit schematics e2e + dry-run-no-write).","tree":{"sha":"6da609f081eac2b49dac15540980d18f650ad01c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/6da609f081eac2b49dac15540980d18f650ad01c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDIyODg0ZGZiNzZkNTA5YTFkOWVmNzdlZTNiYTIyMjRlNzRlODVhYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a","sha":"4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a"}],"sha":"22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/22884dfb76d509a1d9ef77ee3ba2224e74e85aa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T09:44:17Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T09:44:17Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"fix(treaty-ivy): 4 polish residuals — member-decorator strip, i18n byte-exact, dep order, ctor overload\n\nAll measured; default 185/185 + swc 29/29 preserved:\n1. MEMBER-DECORATOR STRIP (source_compile.rs): inert member @HostBinding/@HostListener/\n   @Input/@Output/@ViewChild decorators are now excised from the lowered class (the\n   ɵɵdefineDirective/Component already encodes them; they tripped swc-loader\n   decorators:false). Class still emits the same hostBindings etc.\n2. i18n BYTE-EXACT (template/i18n.rs + both emitters): const naming now matches\n   @angular/compiler exactly — bare i18n_<N> + MSG_<SUFFIX>_<N> (empty path → MSG__0)\n   — and the U+FFFD marker is emitted RAW (removed the escape post-pass in emitter.rs\n   AND emitter_swc.rs). parity.mjs strict: the 2 i18n fixtures are now byte-equal to\n   the oracle (388==388, 553==553). matchGolden stays 185/185 (run-compliance\n   canonicalizer folds the new deterministic names; 12/12 harness self-tests pass).\n3. DEP FLAG ORDER (partial_emit.rs): multi-flag ɵɵngDeclareFactory deps now emit\n   token/attribute/host/optional/self/skipSelf (Angular compileDependency order).\n4. CTOR OVERLOAD (source_compile.rs): factory deps now reflect the IMPLEMENTATION\n   constructor (body-bearing), not the first bodiless overload.\n+5 new tests, all round-tripping through link_partial.","tree":{"sha":"35a53994d791f5b4ed058cf02ffc662e2a760bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/35a53994d791f5b4ed058cf02ffc662e2a760bb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDRhMzQyYmYzODc4MjMxZjQ2NTM2NTM5NDFjYTcwN2FkNDRjZTA4NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314","sha":"f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314"}],"sha":"4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/4a342bf3878231f4653653941ca707ad44ce085a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T08:51:30Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T08:51:30Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): partial-mode completeness — external template, factory DI deps, ngDeclareClassMetadata\n\nCompletes partial mode to match Angular''s own partial compiler (verified field-for-\nfield vs the vendored GOLDEN_PARTIAL.js, all mode-gated; default Full byte-unchanged:\n185/185 + swc 29/29 re-confirmed):\n- EXTERNAL TEMPLATE: a templateUrl/styleUrls component in partial mode now emits\n  ɵɵngDeclareComponent with the host-RESOLVED template inlined as `template` (isInline\n  OMITTED) + resolved styles, matching Angular''s external-resource partial shape.\n  New compile_component_source_with_options_and_resolved, wired in packagr.\n- FACTORY DEPS: ɵɵngDeclareFactory no longer hardcodes deps:[] — factory_deps_from_body\n  DECOMPILES the AOT ɵfac body (ɵɵinject/ɵɵdirectiveInject/ɵɵinjectAttribute +\n  InjectFlags host/self/skipSelf/optional, ɵɵgetInheritedFactory→deps:null,\n  invalidFactory→\"invalid\"); byte-matches the di golden incl the flag matrix.\n- ɵɵngDeclareClassMetadata (new partial_class_metadata.rs): emits the dev-only\n  companion (decorators/ctorParameters/propDecorators verbatim from the class AST),\n  which the linker drops to void 0 — matches ng-packagr; round-trips inertly.\n- 9 new tests + a real-golden gate; all partial output round-trips back to AOT\n  ɵɵdefine* through link_partial (zero residual ngDeclare).\n\nHonest follow-ups (cosmetic, round-trip-safe): (1) multi-flag dep field ORDER for a\nparam with 2+ inject flags should be token/attribute/host/optional/self/skipSelf;\n(2) constructor-overload reflection should use the implementation signature, not the\nfirst bodiless overload.","tree":{"sha":"8985f970004bd6a28795134ccc74d33b37b0b8ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/8985f970004bd6a28795134ccc74d33b37b0b8ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGYwZTFmMjI2NDFmNGFlOWJiYTM4ZGZkYjNhZjIxYWY5MDc1ODUzMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/8e6b9aba8de99bd1e475b6ac5af4ffe9f03d8a0c","sha":"8e6b9aba8de99bd1e475b6ac5af4ffe9f03d8a0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8e6b9aba8de99bd1e475b6ac5af4ffe9f03d8a0c"}],"sha":"f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f0e1f22641f4ae9bba38dfdb3af21af907585314"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8e6b9aba8de99bd1e475b6ac5af4ffe9f03d8a0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T08:29:59Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T08:29:59Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(@treaty/rspack): wire cross-module SelectorRegistry — real app-* apps resolve via rspack too\n\nCompletes real-selector resolution across ALL standard bundlers (vite + rolldown +\nnow rspack). JS-only (no Rust/treaty_ivy/NAPI touched — the addon already exposes the\nregistry, surfaced via @treaty/compiler.prewarmSelectorRegistry):\n- options.ts: a loader-only `selectorRoot` option.\n- loader.ts: rspack/webpack is a pull pipeline with no buildStart, so the per-file\n  loader prewarms the SHARED compiler''s project selector registry ONCE per\n  (compiler, root) via a WeakMap guard (mirrors vite/rolldown''s idempotent\n  buildStart prewarm); selectorRoot is stripped from the compiler options + stableKey\n  so plugin and loader share one prewarmed compiler.\n- plugin.ts: treatyRule forwards selectorRoot into the loader rule.\nStrictly additive: no selectorRoot → no prewarm → byte-identical fold path.\n\nPROVEN: examples/ng-bench-app (non-folding \"app-stat-card\") built via @rspack/core\n2.0.6 + headless-booted → stat cards RENDER (count=3, nonEmpty=3, real signal data),\nvs the A/B control (no selectorRoot) → 3 empty hosts. tsgo clean; rspack smoke 14/14.","tree":{"sha":"1a623ffd01436b409d7dbdfd98827fd48796fa7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/1a623ffd01436b409d7dbdfd98827fd48796fa7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/8e6b9aba8de99bd1e475b6ac5af4ffe9f03d8a0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/