epos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/75ff849f8ad6a548f51ce58a4d6b1744a0301350/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T18:35:35Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T18:35:35Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): real SWC emit backend — byte-identical to oxc (29/29 + full suites)\n\nImplements the SWC emit backend as a NEUTRAL hand-rolled printer over the engine-\nneutral output_ast IR (emitter_swc.rs), reproducing oxc_codegen 0.133''s exact format\n(tab indent, object-multiline-iff->1-prop / array-iff->2-elems, precedence\nparenthesization, start_of_stmt/arrow paren-wrap, double-quote+� escaping,\nJS-canonical numbers, $localize cooked/raw). swc_ecma_codegen was empirically ruled\nout (its Config can''t match oxc''s pretty format), so a neutral printer makes\nbyte-equality STRUCTURAL — the plan''s recommended path for guaranteed parity.\n\n- emitter.rs''s four public emit fns are feature-gated dispatchers: oxc (default) /\n  neutral printer (--features swc). The neutral printer is always compiled so one\n  backend-parity binary diffs both printers via an EmitBackend enum.\n- VERIFIED: `backend-parity --features oxc,swc -- parity` → all 29/29 byte-identical\n  across [oxc, swc], exit 0; core (215) + facade (117, incl 12 real-Angular linker\n  tests) suites pass byte-for-byte under --features swc; oxc default path untouched\n  (treaty_ivy 105+12 green). Scope: EMIT backend only — the swc PARSE front-end\n  (oxc_parser → output_ast) is plan phase 3, not yet ported.","tree":{"sha":"97a25112d943b2d36b3d648c5ce7873968a8b78a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/97a25112d943b2d36b3d648c5ce7873968a8b78a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/75ff849f8ad6a548f51ce58a4d6b1744a0301350","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"