tar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/4bd5dbf3e17db9f5b782d982c1113d21dd0750c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T12:10:52Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T12:17:43Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"test(treaty-ivy): fold equivalent generated-temp spellings in the compliance canonicalizer\n\nThe compliance harness canonicalizer collapses Angular''s `$name$` expect-emit\nplaceholders + `_rN` view-ref suffixes to positional tokens before fragment-\nmatching, so a naming-scheme difference does not masquerade as divergence. Three\ncases still false-negative-DIFFed because treaty_ivy emits MODERN, functionally-\nidentical Ivy whose generated-local SPELLING differs from the legacy-TDB golden:\n\n  - the @switch/@if control-flow temporary: golden `$<Component>_contFlowTmp$` /\n    `$tmp_<level>_<index>$` (both -> ID) vs our unwrapped `tmp_<level>_<index>`.\n  - the @let array/object spread value local: golden `<base>_r<N>` (-> `<base>_R`)\n    vs our `$<base>_<N>$`.\n\nFold both spellings to the canonical token the golden already uses, on BOTH the\ngolden and our emit. SURGICAL: rule (A) matches only the `tmp_<digits>_<digits>`\nscratch name; rule (B) restricts to the spread local uniquely identified as the\nLHS of a `ɵɵpureFunction<N>` assignment and PRESERVES the base name, so distinct\nlocals keep distinct tokens (a swapped/mis-bound read still diverges) and the\nnon-spread storeLet/readContextLet/reference locals — which Angular''s golden\ndeliberately distinguishes — are untouched. Folds NAMES only, never semantics:\na corrupted instruction arg (slot/case index) still DIFFs.\n\nmatchGolden 178/185 -> 181/185 by exactly these 3 cases flipping to PASS, no\npreviously-passing case regresses. Harness-only; no Rust, no goldens changed.","tree":{"sha":"fd4ed0ef2f01915a344b53bfee40947a4021c443","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/fd4ed0ef2f01915a344b53bfee40947a4021c443"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/4bd5dbf3e17db9f5b782d982c1113d21dd0750c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/4bd5dbf3e17db9f5b782d982c1113d21dd0750c6","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDRiZDV