 Api hosting, and now real SSE/WebSocket handlers +\na runnable host (emit_production_host) — verified by a real `cargo build` against\naxum, not just syn::parse. rust_authoring 427 tests.","tree":{"sha":"7341e4e42802f475af1e550fe3ced5189222188e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/7341e4e42802f475af1e550fe3ced5189222188e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/28b9445d8b7cf8a09c08abd9e8c6aad6323f3128","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/28b9445d8b7cf8a09c08abd9e8c6aad6323f3128","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDI4Yjk0NDVkOGI3Y2Y4YTA5YzA4YWJkOWU4YzZhYWQ2MzIzZjMxMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298","sha":"145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298"}],"sha":"28b9445d8b7cf8a09c08abd9e8c6aad6323f3128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/28b9445d8b7cf8a09c08abd9e8c6aad6323f3128"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:35:29Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:48:10Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(authoring): emit a runnable production host for the generated server module\n\nThe axum backend''s emit() ends at `pub fn build_router() -> Router`, a\nlibrary with no main, no async runtime, and no listener -- so a packaged app\ncould compile its server fns but never RUN them in production (dev relied on\nthe Vite middleware). Add `emit_production_host(module, default_port)`, which\nreturns a complete, self-contained main.rs that declares the server module as\na sibling, starts a tokio runtime, resolves the listen port from $PORT (with a\nconfigurable default), binds 0.0.0.0:<port>, and serves build_router() via\naxum::serve.\n\nTests parse the emitted host with syn::parse_file (a real parse, not a regex\nshape check) to prove it is well-formed Rust, verify the tokio/PORT/serve\nwiring and a custom module name + port, and confirm a real generated server\nmodule plus the host both parse and reference the same build_router factory.\nAdds syn as a dev-dependency for that verification.","tree":{"sha":"90b0af82f3fd101db0f413b0317a2def850f8c4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/90b0af82f3fd101db0f413b0317a2def850f8c4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDE0NTY2MGY2N2I1OWQzODc0NjRkYTdiZDQ3NTczZTQzODBjNTcyOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273","sha":"c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273"}],"sha":"145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/145660f67b59d387464da7bd47573e4380c57298"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:55:15Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:48:10Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(authoring): make the axum SSE + WebSocket server-fn handlers real\n\nemit_stream_handler / emit_ws_handler no longer comment out the author body\nand stub an empty stream / echo loop. They now drive the real transport:\n\n- Stream: an `Sse<impl Stream<Item=Result<Event,Infallible>>>` GET handler.\n  The generator body is transpiled with the new yield-aware\n  `transpile_stream_body`, lowering each `yield X` to a push of\n  `serde_json::json!(X)` onto an `__items` accumulator that is mapped into\n  `Event::default().json_data(..)` SSE frames. Params travel in the EventSource\n  URL as a JSON `args` query and bind into typed locals; the client binding now\n  sends them.\n- WebSocket: a `WebSocketUpgrade` GET handler that runs the duplex body — a\n  recv loop that, per Text frame, binds the data params from the frame''s args,\n  runs a generated per-message handler, and sends the JSON response back; Close\n  ends the loop. The body is lowered with the new `transpile_ws_body`, whose\n  `serde_json::json!`-wrapped returns make the result a uniform\n  `serde_json::Value`.\n\nWhere the body can''t fully transpile, the handler still COMPILES: the stream\nwires the transport with a typed placeholder `futures::stream::empty()` and the\nws wires the upgrade + recv loop with a placeholder echo, each preserving the\nauthor body verbatim as a comment — never broken Rust.\n\nTranspiler correctness fixes surfaced by actually compiling the output against\naxum 0.8: numeric for-loops cast their bounds to i64 (a `Range<f64>` is not\niterable) and string `+` lowers to `format!` (`&str + String` does not compile).\n\nTests assert the generated Rust is well-formed (balanced delimiters), drives\nthe yields / recv loop, degrades to a compiling placeholder, and that the\nrouter mounts GET routes for both transports. Verified end-to-end by compiling\na generated module against real axum 0.8.","tree":{"sha":"1182cf2ef973f32c0b4c5301bb74b441f374aff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/1182cf2ef973f32c0b4c5301bb74b441f374aff4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGMyMTdhZWQ1YmE0MjkzOTY1NjNmOWEyYTZlMDA2MGEwMWU5MDAyNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4","sha":"8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4"}],"sha":"c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/c217aed5ba429396563f9a2a6e0060a01e900273"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:09:16Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:09:16Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"docs: matchGolden 178/185 + record the roadmap climb (compliance, FESM, real Api hosting)\n\nThree genuine compliance DIFFs closed (forward-ref import thunks, @defer lazy\ndependency-resolver fns, @defer linked into i18n messages) — 175→178/185, zero\nregression. FESM flattening + the real production axum Api handler also landed; SSE/WS\n+ runnable host are being rebased onto the Api-handler base. README parity 175→178.","tree":{"sha":"5fdeee8e9c042de5712dc7f02c00f7dfd053039b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/5fdeee8e9c042de5712dc7f02c00f7dfd053039b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDhlMWM2MThjNDg5NzA1YzNmOGNkYzMwMTFmNWViZjYxMDUyZDlmYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f","sha":"f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f"}],"sha":"8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8e1c618c489705c3f8cdc3011f5ebf61052d9fc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:44:36Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:06:38Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(authoring): make the production axum Api handler generation real (deserialize, run body, Json response)\n\nThe default axum backend now emits a handler that genuinely deserializes the\nrequest struct, RUNS the (transpiled or rust-verbatim) body, and returns\nJson<RESP> — not a body whose return type mismatches the signature.\n\nemit_handler:\n  * derives -> Json<RESP> from the fn''s mapped return type\n  * lowers ts bodies via the new transpile_handler_body, which wraps every\n    `return EXPR` into the handler''s Json<RESP> shape and only appends a\n    trailing typed default when control can fall through (no unreachable tail)\n  * a ts body outside the supported subset degrades to a clearly-marked,\n    COMPILING typed-default stub (original TS kept as a comment) — never broken\n    Rust\n  * rust-verbatim bodies pass through with a Json(Default::default()) fall-through\n\nts_to_rust transpiler — cover the common server-fn shapes:\n  * object literals -> serde_json::json!({ ... }) (object returns)\n  * array literals  -> serde_json::json!([ ... ])\n  * template literals -> format!(\"...{}\", ...)\n  * string `+` concatenation -> format! (so it yields a real String)\n  * ternary ?:, unary -/!, computed index a[b], null literal\n  * ts_type_to_rust: unwrap AsyncGenerator/Generator/Iterable<T> + T|undefined\n    nullable unions (the stream/maybe-return shapes)\n  * db-ish/unknown dependency calls pass through by name; an uncovered ts body\n    keys the whole handler to the typed-default stub so it always compiles\n\nTests: assert the GENERATED Rust is well-formed by parsing it as a real\nsyn::File (added as a dev-dependency already present in the lockfile), plus\ngolden-string checks that the handler deserializes the request, wraps returns\nin Json, and that build_router() mounts the POST /__server/<name> route.\nVerified the emitted modules also type-check against real axum 0.7 + serde.","tree":{"sha":"d9fd8bc7c44a7bf5baf49d63f1afaeae0b73d747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/d9fd8bc7c44a7bf5baf49d63f1afaeae0b73d747"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGYwMjIyMDk5ZjQyN2Q0MWFhNGEzYmY3YjQzZDViOTFlODZjMmEzMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3","sha":"877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3"}],"sha":"f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f0222099f427d41aa4a3bf7b43d5b91e86c2a32f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:47:12Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:04:49Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): link @defer blocks into i18n messages faithfully\n\nTwo gaps made the `r3_view_compiler_i18n/blocks/should support @defer\nblocks` compliance case DIFF against Angular''s golden:\n\n1. The `@defer` START_BLOCK `original_code` was hardcoded to the bare\n   `@defer {`, dropping the trigger clause. Angular records the authored\n   opener verbatim (`i18n_parser.ts::visitBlock` ->\n   `block.startSourceSpan.toString()`), i.e. `@defer (when isLoaded) {`.\n   The view layer only carries offset spans, so reconstruct the opener\n   from the trigger AST (like `if_branch_header`/the `@for` header),\n   covering `when`/`on …`/`prefetch`/`hydrate` trigger forms.\n\n2. The `@defer` main/placeholder/loading/error views were built without\n   the i18n sub-template continuation, so their bodies emitted raw\n   text/element ops (decls 4) instead of the i18n-collapsed\n   `ɵɵi18nStart(0, msg, subIdx)` + `ɵɵelement` (decls 2). Thread the\n   `I18nChildView` into each defer view in view-creation order (main,\n   loading, placeholder, error), matching the sentinel resolver''s\n   sub-template numbering, exactly as `@if` branches already do.\n\nCompliance matchGolden 175/185 -> 176/185; no other case regresses. All\ntreaty_ivy crate tests stay green.","tree":{"sha":"11bc77207237695458b3b5b4c4e58e273568474a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/11bc77207237695458b3b5b4c4e58e273568474a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDg3N2I4ZGE0YjA5ZGZiYzY2NDNiZjAzNjJjYjVjNWQyOTYzZTlhYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5","sha":"463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5"}],"sha":"877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/877b8da4b09dfbc6643bf0362cb5c5d2963e9ab3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:00:50Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:03:54Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): generate @defer per-block lazy dependency resolver fns\n\nImplements the missing `@defer` dependency resolver emit so a directive used\nonly inside a `@defer` block''s main body is lazy-loaded rather than eagerly\nreferenced.\n\n- compute_defer_dependencies (facade/compile.rs): re-runs the selectorless +\n  CSS-selector matching passes over the eager projection (template with every\n  @defer MAIN body emptied) and over each block''s main body, yielding the eager\n  set and per-block lazy dep lists. Mirrors ngtsc getEagerlyUsedDirectives /\n  resolveDeferBlocks (the binder is already @defer-aware: placeholder/loading/\n  error views are eager, only the main body is lazy).\n- compile_component_meta (source_compile.rs): drops lazy-only deps from the\n  runtime `dependencies` array and builds R3ComponentDeferMetadata::PerBlock with\n  one `() => [Dep, ...]` resolver thunk per block (compileDeferResolverFunction;\n  local non-deferrable deps emit as a bare type reference).\n- build_deferred_block (template/view/template.rs): hoists each resolver as a\n  top-level `const <Base>_Defer_<slot>_DepsFn = ...` and passes the reference as\n  the third `ɵɵdefer(slot, mainSlot, resolverFn, ...)` argument. Threaded via a\n  span-keyed map through TemplateCompilationInput / TemplateBuilder.\n\nEmit now matches Angular for deferred_with_local_deps:\n  const MyApp_Defer_4_DepsFn = () => [LazyDep];\n  ɵɵdefer(4, 2, MyApp_Defer_4_DepsFn, 3);\n  dependencies: [EagerDep, LoadingDep]   // LazyDep dropped\n\nThe compliance canonicalizer gains a STRICT fold for the @defer DepsFn\nConstantPool shared-function reference (the identical case as the existing _cN\nshared-literal fold): the goldens spell this renamable pool reference as the\n`$..._DepsFn$` expect-emit placeholder, so map our REAL literal pool name to the\nsame ID token. Matches only the exact <Ident>_Defer_<digits>_DepsFn token.\n\nmatchGolden 175/185 -> 176/185; no regressions.","tree":{"sha":"a9a56d66037a3b0380e8d9a9b43973165afbec42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/a9a56d66037a3b0380e8d9a9b43973165afbec42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDQ2M2FkOGEyOTFjY2E4NDdmNjVmYzU3YzNhM2RmMjgwMDAwOWQ2YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3","sha":"f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3"}],"sha":"463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/463ad8a291cca847f65fc57c3a3df2800009d6c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:45:33Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T11:02:47Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(treaty-ivy): closure-wrap forward-referenced component dependencies\n\nA standalone component''s `dependencies` array must be emitted as a lazy\n`() => [...]` thunk (Angular `DeclarationListEmitMode.Closure`) instead of a\ndirect `[...]` array whenever a referenced class may be forward-declared, so the\nbinding is read only after the whole module has initialised. The source\nfront-end previously hardcoded `Direct`, so it mis-compiled the\n`forwardRef(() => X)` standalone-import case as `dependencies: [X]`.\n\nSet `Closure` when EITHER condition Angular checks holds:\n  * a standalone component''s `imports:` carries a literal `forwardRef(() => …)`\n    entry (`standaloneImportMayBeForwardDeclared`), OR\n  * an emitted dependency class is declared LATER in the same file than the\n    component (`isExpressionForwardReference`: `context.pos < node.pos`); a\n    self-referential recursive component is NOT forward (strict `<`).\n\nThreads a per-file class-name -> source-start-offset map through `CompileCtx`\nso the component path can compare each dependency''s position against its own.\n\nFixes the compliance DIFF \"standalone/should handle a forwardRef in the imports\nof a standalone component\"; matchGolden 175 -> 176, no regressions.","tree":{"sha":"7f195c825d7c77637395562468cc97330590c5b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/7f195c825d7c77637395562468cc97330590c5b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKGY4Y2NhMTlkNGQyYmUxMmIzZTNmZTVhYmJkZWI4MTYxNDJhNjA1YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc","sha":"8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc"}],"sha":"f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f8cca19d4d2be12b3e3fe5abbdeb816142a605b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:49:21Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T10:50:41Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"feat(packagr): flatten each entry to an APF FESM module (oxc inliner)\n\nAdd a FESM flattening step that, for every entry, resolves the package''s\nown PRIVATE relative imports (`./x`, `../y` that are not themselves\npublished entry points), inlines them deps-first into one flat ES module,\nand de-dupes/hoists bare specifiers (`@angular/*`, `tslib`, npm deps) as\nexternal imports — the APF fesm2022 shape. Built as a self-contained\noxc-based internal-module inliner (libs/packagr/src/fesm.rs); no external\nbundler.\n\nThe inliner is span-based, so emitted Ivy bytes (`ɵɵdefineComponent`,\n`ɵfac`/`ɵcmp`) are preserved verbatim. Relative imports of sibling\npublished entries are left untouched (secondary entries are separate FESM\nfiles in APF), so a pure re-export barrel — and any single-file component\n— flattens to a byte-for-byte identity.\n\nCorrectness is guarded: concatenation only proceeds when top-level binding\nnames do not collide across the merged modules; a collision, an import\ncycle, a default/namespace import of an inlined module, a dependency\ncompile error, or a failed re-parse/leak-check all bail to identity, so\nflattening never corrupts an entry.\n\nDistEntry.esm now carries the flattened module — the exact bytes emitted as\neach entry''s index.mjs and pointed at by the manifest''s module/exports —\nkeeping the stable per-entry layout.\n\nTests: existing package_treaty_shadcn + package_real_library stay green\n(identity path); new fesm_inlines_internal_module proves a private helper\nis inlined (no surviving relative import, re-parses, keeps\nɵɵdefineComponent, externals preserved) while a sibling entry stays a\nseparate module; unit tests cover inline, collision-bail, default-import\nbail, and sibling-untouched.","tree":{"sha":"b6025d9653de9ea136f936c5632425241bf71ae3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/b6025d9653de9ea136f936c5632425241bf71ae3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/commits/8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc","node_id":"C_kwDOLhfoE9oAKDhiYWZiM2QxZmYzYmFjODBjYTE2OWFiYzI1OTQ3YTZiNTIyMGI3Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/treatyjs/treaty/commit/f87d1331f1aad91bd47eab91665fab31b7120341","sha":"f87d1331f1aad91bd47eab91665fab31b7120341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f87d1331f1aad91bd47eab91665fab31b7120341"}],"sha":"8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/8bafb3d1ff3bac80ca169abc25947a6b5220b7cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2092344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Jordan-Hall","id":2092344,"login":"Jordan-Hall","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTIzNDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jordan-Hall","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/commits/f87d1331f1aad91bd47eab91665fab31b7120341/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T09:29:04Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T09:29:04Z","email":"Jordan@libertyware.co.uk","name":"Jordan Upton"},"message":"ci: add a Rust-test workflow (workspace + the excluded file-routing crate)\n\nThe only CI was a GitHub Pages deploy of the REPL — no test run existed. Add a\nworkflow that runs `cargo test --workspace` (the link-gate integration test now skips\ncleanly on a bare CI checkout, so no npm install needed) AND, separately,\n`cargo test --manifest-path libs/file-routing/Cargo.toml` — the file-routing crate is\n`exclude`d from the workspace (so the NAPI addon can path-depend on it), so its ~90\ntests were never run in CI. Closes the T2 coverage hole.","tree":{"sha":"35463854862e9467044981eeb179e81934196b53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/trees/35463854862e9467044981eeb179e81934196b53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/treatyjs/treaty/git/co