ons_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/commits/a545f99eca14a894d4ce58168ee73afa4e819e00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T16:20:11Z","email":"rafi.adnan@optimizely.com","name":"Rafi Adnan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:37:43Z","email":"rafiadnan47@gmail.com","name":"Rafi Adnan"},"message":"feat(mcp): add createServer() factory\n\nEvery tool was registered on one module-level McpServer. An McpServer holds one transport at a time, and the SDK forbids reusing a stateless HTTP transport across requests, so an HTTP host needs a server per request. Opal worked around this by queueing requests on the shared instance.\n\ncreateServer() builds a fresh McpServer with every tool registered. The data import stays at module level, so instances share the loaded data and creating one is cheap. The `server` export is kept as createServer()''s result for existing programmatic users.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"553d788503d9c305708f76931f177d6b7705e844","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/git/trees/553d788503d9c305708f76931f177d6b7705e844"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/git/commits/a545f99eca14a894d4ce58168ee73afa4e819e00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/758244?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/radnan","id":758244,"login":"radnan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1ODI0NA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/commit/a545f99eca14a894d4ce58168ee73afa4e819e00","node_id":"C_kwDOLmk80NoAKGE1NDVmOTllY2ExNGE4OTRkNGNlNTgxNjhlZTczYWZhNGU4MTllMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/commit/3d80b7d0e8ad9f38fe78aaf1a5cbf21526d8a787","sha":"3d80b7d0e8ad9f38fe78aaf1a5cbf21526d8a787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/commits/3d80b7d0e8ad9f38fe78aaf1a5cbf21526d8a787"}],"sha":"a545f99eca14a894d4ce58168ee73afa4e819e00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/commits/a545f99eca14a894d4ce58168ee73afa4e819e00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43566487?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toha993","id":43566487,"login":"toha993","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTY2NDg3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toha993","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/commits/3d80b7d0e8ad9f38fe78aaf1a5cbf21526d8a787/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:28:25Z","email":"mutasim.toha@optimizely.com","name":"toha993"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:28:27Z","email":"rafiadnan47@gmail.com","name":"Rafi Adnan"},"message":"fix(react): reorder tall Sortable items by overlap\n\nWith clone feedback the source keeps its full-size rect, and pointer\nintersection kept it as the drop target until the pointer left it. With a\nhandle near the top, dragging a tall item down needed almost its full\nheight before neighbors swapped.\n\nUse shapeIntersection for items so the swap follows how much the clone\noverlaps each item. SortableGroup keeps its own detector, so column\ntargeting is unchanged. Add a TallItems story whose play test fails\nwithout this change.","tree":{"sha":"d7f3038d709026700199de41ac462b2300f1e87d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/git/trees/d7f3038d709026700199de41ac462b2300f1e87d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/optimizely-axiom/optiaxiom/git/commits/3d80b7d0e8ad9f38fe78aaf1a5cbf21526d8a787","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/758244?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radnan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_